; A byte-string literal (`h'…'`, and the UTF-8 spelling `'…'`) as a fixed MEMBER value. The value is
; fixed by the schema and `FixedValue` has no bytes variant, so there is nothing for the member to
; hold — REJECTED GRACEFULLY at `rust_type_from_type2`'s member/element catch-all, the role-sibling
; of the rule-body catch-all in `parse_type`.
;
; The catalog row guards the ABORT direction specifically: this arm replaced a blanket
; `panic!("Ignoring Type2: …")` that covered every unrepresentable member type2 at once, so a
; regression would take the whole family down with it. Per-construct message identity is pinned by
; `unsupported_member_type2_rejects_gracefully` (src/tests/robustness_tests.rs), which also covers
; the unkeyed-element and map-value paths into the same arm.
;
; Widening the member to `bytes` generates, but no longer constrains the value to the literal — a
; different spec, not an equivalent one — which is why this is a refusal and not a silent widening.
a = [v: h'0102', x: uint]
